{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>For every matter [he shall be] free</b> — that he be free in speech, as that which we say: everyone knows why a bride enters the wedding canopy, etc. Another interpretation: <b>for every matter [he shall be] free</b> for his house — that one who marries a woman is forgiven for all his sins." "<b>[He shall be] free for his house one year</b> — Sefer Torah: the Name of four letters, to teach that HaShem testifies about them and declares their union permitted. And <b>and rejoice</b> — whence [derive] the days of <b>and rejoice</b>: he is obligated in conjugal relations throughout the year, all the days of the year except Yom HaKippurim. The verse begins with <b>When a man takes</b> and ends with <b>taking</b>, to teach: one who marries a woman in his youth — he marries a woman in his old age: <b>his wife whom he has taken</b>. And adjacent to it: <b>He shall not take a pledge</b>, to teach: he shall not withhold his wife from conjugal relations. Another interpretation: because the wife is the pledge of a person, for on account of the sin of vows a man's wife dies."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:10:34.702534532Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}